{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AAO REVIEWS - page bootstrap
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Rendered once from layout/theme.liquid. Emits the widget stylesheet, the engine and the runtime
config. The engine bails out immediately (and never fetches the review data) on pages that hold
neither a `.aao-reviews` widget nor a `.aao-rating` badge, so this is cheap sitewide.

Endpoints live on the agency VPS:
  submitUrl    POST {handle, rating, author, email, text} -> {"ok": true}
  approvedUrl  GET  the same products-map schema as assets/aao-reviews.json, merged over it

Set `inline_data: true` when rendering to embed the whole baked dataset in the page instead of
letting the browser fetch it. That gives a server-rendered, crawlable copy of every review at the
cost of the full JSON on every page, so it is off by default. See docs/reviews/README.md.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign submit_url = 'https://allign.agency/aao/reviews/submit'
  assign approved_url = 'https://allign.agency/aao/reviews/approved.json'
-%}

{{ 'aao-reviews.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<script>
  window.AAO_REVIEWS_CONFIG = {
    assetUrl: {{ 'aao-reviews.json' | asset_url | json }},
    submitUrl: {{ submit_url | json }},
    approvedUrl: {{ approved_url | json }}
  };
</script>

{%- if inline_data -%}
  <script type="application/json" id="aao-reviews-data">{{ 'aao-reviews.json' | inline_asset_content }}</script>
{%- endif -%}

<script src="{{ 'aao-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
